{"step_index":165,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:35:13Z","thinking":"**Verifying Stationary Ball Lemma**\n\nExamining the statement: if the $(k+1)$-radius ball around $v$ is the same as the $k$-radius ball, then all further balls $(k+m)$-radius are also the same as the $k$-radius ball. The goal is to establish this stationary property for the ball. The lemma `ballWithin_stationary_succ` seems relevant.\n```lean\nlemma ballWithin_stationary_succ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n    (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) (m : ℕ) :\n    ballWithin G (k + m) v = ballWithin G k v :=\n```\n\n\n**Proving Stationary Property Implications**\n\nProved the base lemma through induction, showing that if `ballWithin G (k+1) v = ballWithin G k v`, then all further balls are equal to the k-radius ball. This leads to the conclusion that if the $(k+1)$-radius ball equals the $k$-radius ball, the $k$-radius ball is the entire universe, `univ`.\n\nThe contrapositive of this implication is that if `ballWithin G k v` is not the whole universe, the $(k+1)$-radius ball must be different from the $k$-radius ball. Since the radius increases, this implies a strict increase in cardinality of the ball.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_card_bound.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\nopen GraphCalc\\n\\nlemma ballWithin_subset_succ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V) :\\n    ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\\n  intro x hx\\n  dsimp [ballWithin]\\n  exact Finset.mem_union_left _ hx\\n\\nlemma ballWithin_subset_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k m : ℕ) (v : V) :\\n    ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + m) v := by\\n  induction m with\\n  | zero => exact subset_refl _\\n  | succ m ih =>\\n    have h1 := ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + m) v\\n    exact ih.trans h1\\n\\nlemma ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\\n    (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) (m : ℕ) :\\n    ballWithin G (k + m) v = ballWithin G k v := by\\n  induction m with\\n  | zero => rfl\\n  | succ m ih =>\\n    have heq : k + (m + 1) = (k + m) + 1 := by omega\\n    rw [heq]\\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\\n    rw [ih]\\n    exact h\\n\\nlemma ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G)\\n    (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) :\\n    ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ := by\\n  have h_add := ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add G k v h (Fintype.card V)\\n  have h_sub : ballWithin G (Fintype.card V) v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + Fintype.card V) v := by\\n    have heq : k + Fintype.card V = Fintype.card V + k := by omega\\n    rw [heq]\\n    exact ballWithin_subset_add G (Fintype.card V) k v\\n  rw [hrad v] at h_sub\\n  rw [h_add] at h_sub\\n  exact Finset.eq_univ_of_univ_subset h_sub\\n\\nlemma card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [De\n<truncated 562 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Write test_card_bound.lean\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
